ond term is $-2g,$\n\n- the third term is $-15h.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the third term. The third term is $-15h.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444247 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444247 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444247 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444247 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the expression $-2p+3q-5r?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e6d4984-6930-5fe6-93df-11f6e79d298e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444247 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression $-2p+3q-5r$ has three terms:  $-2p$, $3q$, and $-5r.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n3q-5r-2p.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444248 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444248 #edb/ref 1069 "q-4992" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444248 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444248 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the individual terms of the expression $p-2q+3r?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444248 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c80bb1e-f4d1-5e69-a3bf-0a3439a01237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444248 #edb/ref 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(p)+(-2q)+(3r)\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the expression has three terms:  $p$, $-2q$, and $3r.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444249 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444249 #edb/ref 1069 "q-176831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444249 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444249 #edb/ref 1071 "The third term of the expression $8-\\frac{3}{4}a-\\frac{4}{5}b+2c$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4cf8dfa1-a016-55ee-948f-099f977c00ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444249 #edb/ref 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(8)+(-\\frac{3}{4}a)+(-\\frac{4}{5}b)+(2c)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $8,$\n\n- the second term is $-\\frac{3}{4}a,$\n\n- the third term is $-\\frac{4}{5}b,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $2c.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the third term. The third term is $-\\frac{4}{5}b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444250 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444250 #edb/ref 1069 "q-176829" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444250 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444250 #edb/ref 1071 "The fourth term of the expression $7u-2v-0.3w+10x$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444250 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53c72840-d479-512c-a2f9-7b59b04f5d7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444250 #edb/ref 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(7u)+(-2v)+(-0.3w)+(10x)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $7u,$\n\n- the second term is $-2v,$\n\n- the third term is $-0.3w,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $10x.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the fourth term. The fourth term is $10x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444251 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444251 #edb/ref 1069 "q-176816" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444251 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444251 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the terms of the expression $7k-5l?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444251 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99c23d7a-4cde-50f0-9ab0-eeb0b55149d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444251 #edb/ref 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(7k)+(-5l)\n$$\n\nSo, the expression has two terms:  $7k$ and $-5l.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444252 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 1759218644