ression $x+y+z?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444254 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dc6f69af-3519-5e1e-a844-300430273bdd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444254 #edb/ref 1074 "There are three terms in the expression: $x$, $y$ and $z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444255 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444255 #edb/ref 1069 "q-4987" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444255 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444255 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the terms of the expression $2d-9e+5f+11?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444255 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5a18a8b-2e65-5f13-8c6c-7e826fcaa6ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444255 #edb/ref 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(2d)+(-9e)+(5f)+(11)\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the expression has four terms:  $2d$, $-9e$, $5f$, and $11.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174099" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1071 "Create an expression equivalent to $3x-2y+4z-3w:$\n\n$3x-2y+4z-3w=$\n{{field-1}}\n$w\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$y\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}\n$z$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f72b7910-f317-5fd4-bdc7-ea9bd6020aca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444256 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression $3x-2y+4z-3w$ has four terms: $3x$, $-2y$, $4z$, and $-3w.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n-3w-2y+3x+4z.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
